Interview with the Wizard      NannyMUD Times                        Page 11
Drelic

  Greetings Drelic, welcome to another NannyMUD Times interview.

  A: Thank you.

  A view of Drelic's workroom:
  *--------------------------------------------------------------------------*
  | You're in Drelic's small and messy cabin. There's drawings and tools all |
  | over the place. There's a big work bench in the middle of the room, full |
  | of cog-wheels and strange devices. A flickering lamp hangs from the      |
  | ceiling, spreading light over the room. Six brightly shining portals can |
  | be found in the eastern wall.                                            |
  | There are six obvious exits: church, area, post, guild, examples and     |
  |           wizroom.                                                       |
  *--------------------------------------------------------------------------*

  Drelic smiles happily.

  Q: Care to share your real name?

  A: Why not? My real name is Fredrik Larsson.
     Yes, I'm a swede.

  Q: What's your players age?

  A: He's 273 days young.

  Q: When did you start playing NannyMUD?

  A: I logged on for the first time in '98, I think, when a friend from
     another MUD showed it to me. As I was playing actively on another
     MUD back then, I didn't really play that much on Nanny at first...
     I think I started playing "actively" on Nanny in '99 or so.

  Q: What guild did you start in?

  A: Drelic hmms.
     Oh my, I think it was Druids. I know I was a member of both the
     Druids and the Assembly with my very first character, I just can't
     remember in which order :)

  Q: Was Drelic your first character?

  A: Drelic shakes his head.
     He was not. Drelic was born the 25th of April, 2000.
     I had one or two characters that I used to play back then.
     This was the first one I _really_ played with, tho.

  Q: What guild was Drelic?

  A: He was a Knight :)

  Q: Did you become a wizard as a knight?

  A: Drelic shakes his head.
     I guess I wanted to see something else before I became immortal :P
     Drelic grins evilly.

  Q: What guild did you become a wizard in?

  A: As a Viking, I believe. I joined and left a few guilds before I
     finally became a wiz. I wanted to play around a bit before it
     finally happened.

  Q: When did you become a wizard?

  A: Hold on, let me search through my memory data bank :)
     May 2004, it seems.

  Q: Are you going to create an area?

  A: As a matter of fact, I'm in the middle of the creation process of
     one as we speak.

  Q: Tell us what your area is going to be like.

  A: Well, I've made the kind of area I'd like to visit myself. I've
     tried to set a mood with the descriptions, the monsters and
     everything that comes with it. The pure hack'n'slashers might not
     like it (hopefully they will), as I don't have twenty level 19
     mobs to kill, but the explorers, and the every-bit-of-everythings
     will hopefully enjoy it. Even more so when I get the chance to
     expand the area. My plan is to create a place where every action
     has a reaction, where every step you take leads to something new
     and unexplored. I don't want my area to be yet another place you
     can visit once and know everything about it, I want it to evolve
     constantly.

  Q: That sounds interesting, when do you think it will be finished?

  A: Well, the first part of the area will hopefully be up for approval
     anytime now, if everything goes as planned. If and when that
     happens, I'll hopefully be ready to expand almost instantly.

  Q: Where do you think it will be located?

  A: I haven't really thought about exactly where I'd like it yet, as
     I've been busy focusing on the creation of the area. So if any of
     you readers know an empty space in a forest somewhere, give me a
     call :)

  Q: So, your area will have a forest setting?

  A: Well, there will also be a small village in it. It's not really a
     normal village tho, which the players will find out once I get it
     opened :)

  Q: Do you still play mortal chars?

  A: Indeed I do. Very much so :)
     I think every creating wizard should play his mortals every now
     and then. That way, you'll know what you'd like to see in an area.

  Q: Have you ever had a character banished or demoted?

  A: Drelic coughs noisily, clears his throat and whistles appreciatively.

  Q: Do you have any favourite adventures or killing sprees that you
     remember that you would like to tell us about?

  A: The first thing that comes to mind is that one time, back in the
     days, when I had some real troubles with a quest. I really
     couldn't figure out something, and almost gave up. Then the
     following night, I had a dream about the quest (yes, geeky, I
     know, shut up :P), where I managed to solve the problem. When I
     woke up, I tried to do it the way I had in the dream, just for the
     heck of it, and it actually worked! That felt pretty cool, and it
     has been one of my favourite memories ever since :)

  Q: Do think think NannyMUD needs to more newbie friendly?

  A: I don't think that Nanny in itself needs to be more newbie
     friendly. I think the newbie booklet takes care of that. What we
     do need, however, is to get our players to be more helpful to the
     new, wee ones. I've often seen players shout for help and such,
     only to get mocking responses in return.

  Q: Do you have any ideas on how to get more players into the MUD?

  A: By being more active in advertising, like on sites such as
     mudconnect.com, would be a great start. That site is still
     frequently visited by people looking for new MUDs, even though
     MUDs' popularity aren't as big as a decade ago. You can write your
     own reviews if you like, and read about other MUDs. I think it
     might be hard to get totally MUD-inexperienced people to start
     playing (however not impossible) these days, with all the MMORPGs
     around, so we might have to start looking for people who already
     play somewhere else, who's looking for something new.

  Q: Any final comments for our readers?

  A: All I want to say is this: When I get my area opened, please stop
     by and check it out. I'll keep on working on it, so there will,
     hopefully, always be new things to explore, fight and puzzle out
     :)

  Thank you for taking the time to answers our questions, we look forward
  to seeing your area in the game.

  A: It was a pleasure :)

